        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_977071035.1",
        "comments": "The assembly drPotAngl1.hap1.1 is based on 59x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The species looks to be octoploid (2n = 56), but works as a functional diploid. We can observe high similarity levels within the pairs of chromosomes in each set of the 8 chromosomes, suggesting the chromosomes within each pair are those which really recombine. We can clearly see two distinct genome patterns, based on the HiC signal, indicating that the species is allotetraploid and came from the breeding of two tetraploid species.",
